(3893328, 547809, 69325, '<td valign="top">man i sure am tired of people who get a ribbon on their first entry! j/k nice shot here</td>', 'man i sure am tired of people who get a ribbon on their first entry! j/k nice shot here', '2007-07-11 11:56:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(3893356, 547366, 35994, '<td valign="top">Absolutely amazing colors, LOVE the lizard sitting there. Congrats on a well deserved blue!</td>', 'Absolutely amazing colors, LOVE the lizard sitting there. Congrats on a well deserved blue!', '2007-07-11 12:05:18.000000', NULL, 0),
(3893385, 547905, 49388, '<td valign="top">Congratulations, even though I voted low on this one and theres still something that bothers me, its still a good shot and I would rething my vote if done again.</td>', 'Congratulations, even though I voted low on this one and theres still something that bothers me, its still a good shot and I would rething my vote if done again.', '2007-07-11 12:11:47.000000', NULL, 0),
(3893391, 548046, 63269, '<td valign="top">Well... I saw some of the commenters didn''t like the color, but IMO there''s not at all too much red. This is a very interesting color. Instead, I think the problem might be that the light is sort of over-exposed and the contrast is a little harsh... But I''m not really sure how you could have fixed this. If you had darkened the photo so that the sky was exposed right, then the neat details of the city in the distance would have been lost in shadow.  Perhaps if you could have found a way to shoot the picture without the sun this might have worked better. Or you could just crop the sun out. But I really like the combination of tree-tops and telephone wires on the horizon... it creates a very interesting feeling when you look at it. Great job!</td>', 'Well... I saw some of the commenters didn''t like the color, but IMO there''s not at all too much red. This is a very interesting color. Instead, I think the problem might be that the light is sort of over-exposed and the contrast is a little harsh... But I''m not really sure how you could have fixed this. If you had darkened the photo so that the sky was exposed right, then the neat details of the city in the distance would have been lost in shadow.  Perhaps if you could have found a way to shoot the picture without the sun this might have worked better. Or you could just crop the sun out. But I really like the combination of tree-tops and telephone wires on the horizon... it creates a very interesting feeling when you look at it. Great job!', '2007-07-11 12:14:04.000000', NULL, 0),
(3893467, 547502, 66952, '<td valign="top">Beautiful. Very haunting. Congratulations on the 4th!</td>', 'Beautiful. Very haunting. Congratulations on the 4th!', '2007-07-11 12:27:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(3893537, 547317, 67697, '<td valign="top">Hi Jon - you are so lucky to have places like this to take pictures of.  I''ll assume it is an older church with lots of history behind it.  One thing you may want to try is to move a bit closer to the church where you would still have the building in view but get more of the landscape too.  However, since this challenge is now over, it would really be interesting to see more pics of the church!<br/> <br/>Oh, and nice greens.  :p</td>', 'Hi Jon - you are so lucky to have places like this to take pictures of.  I''ll assume it is an older church with lots of history behind it.  One thing you may want to try is to move a bit closer to the church where you would still have the building in view but get more of the landscape too.  However, since this challenge is now over, it would really be interesting to see more pics of the church! Oh, and nice greens.  :p', '2007-07-11 12:39:45.000000', NULL, 0),
(3893858, 546271, 71550, '<td valign="top">This is going into my faves!</td>', 'This is going into my faves!', '2007-07-11 13:49:42.000000', NULL, 0);
